`std.heap.smp_allocator` (`std.heap.SmpAllocator`) is the recommended general-purpose allocator for `ReleaseFast` when multithreading is enabled. It is designed for `-OReleaseFast` and is intended for fast, production-grade allocation.

For a typical allocator selection:

```zig
const allocator = switch (builtin.mode) {
    .Debug, .ReleaseSafe => debug_allocator.allocator(),
    .ReleaseFast, .ReleaseSmall => std.heap.smp_allocator,
};
```

`SmpAllocator` is a process-wide singleton, so only one should be instantiated per process.
